  "goodToKnow": "Der Neandertaler is a Neanderthal. The species is named after the Neandertal, a valley near Düsseldorf, where quarry workers found bones in 1856. The Swedish geneticist Svante Pääbo, working at the Max Planck Institute in Leipzig, sequenced its genome and won the 2022 Nobel Prize; people of non-African descent carry about 1–2 percent Neanderthal DNA. As an insult, Neandertaler means a brute. The plural is the same."
